course: dictionary
lesson: 708
title: Barbed: sharp hooks and sharp words
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Barbed means having barbs, which are small sharp points or hooks that face backwards. Barbs catch and hold on, so they are hard to pull out, like a fish hook. Barbs grip. They do not just poke.
explain: Barbed has a second meaning for words. A barbed remark is a comment that is unkind and meant to hurt. Use the context to decide which meaning fits: is the text talking about a sharp thing, or about a mean comment?
explain: «A honeybee leaves its barbed stinger in the skin and dies after stinging.» The clue is leaves and stays stuck in the skin. The barbs hold the sting in place, so it cannot come out easily. Swap in your meaning: "a sting with sharp backward points" still makes sense, so barbed means sharp backward points here.
fact: Barbed means having barbs, which are small sharp points or hooks that face backwards.
fact: A «barbed remark» is an unkind comment that is meant to hurt.
fact: «Barbed wire» is fence wire with sharp twisted points, so do not climb over or through it.
fact: A honeybee's «barbed stinger» gets stuck in thick skin and tears away, so the bee dies.
fact: «Porcupines» have «barbed quills» that come out easily when touched and stick into an attacker.
exercise: «A honeybee leaves its barbed stinger in the skin and dies after stinging.» What does barbed mean here? | Shiny and gold | Very long and bendy | Smooth and soft like a wasp's sting | *Having small sharp backward points that hold it in place
exercise: Why should you not climb through barbed wire? | It is soft and warm to hold | It glows in the dark | *It has sharp points that cut skin and clothes | It is too short to climb
exercise: Which animal has barbed quills? | *Porcupine | Chinchilla | Hazel dormouse | Wasp
test: What is barbed wire? | *Wire with sharp twisted points, used around farms | Soft wire used to tie flowers | Wire that glows in the dark | A kind of rope for climbing
test: Which animal's barbed sting gets stuck in thick skin and tears away? | Porcupine | *Honeybee | Wasp | Chinchilla
exam: In «a barbed remark», what does barbed mean? | Glowing with light | Very long and thin | Covered in sharp backward hooks | *Unkind and meant to hurt
